    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d751">

                <pb facs="0926" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.1211/265</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Far Eastern Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief
                        of the Division of Mexican Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-25">November 25, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Johnson</hi>: Taking into consideration a large
                    number of factors, and giving special weight to the fact that the tension
                    between the United States and Japan has been substantially diminished during the
                    past six months and seems in a fair way to further diminution, <pb facs="0927"
                        n="839" xml:id="pg839"/> I feel that we should take no steps whatever with
                    regard to the matter reported upon in the papers hereunder<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d751-f1"/> except to keep the record of everything relating to it
                    strictly confidential (but not to be forgotten).</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ornbeck</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d751-f1" n="54" xml:id="d751-f1-content">
                <p>i. e., despatch No. 2255, February 7, from the Ambassador in Mexico, <ref
                        target="#pg830">p. 830</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
